Z||000000||Ed||02-14-2000||10:14 PM||||Take a look at Click and Clack's website, cartalk.cars.com.  You do listen to Click and Clack on the radio, don't you?  Anyway, They've set up a "worst car of the millenium" site.  Fieros appear pretty frequently.  I'm sure others of your favorites will appear also, as one of my favorite cars, the Corvair, appears about as often. I had a '64 Monza which I ran up to 127,000 miles. Some of the complaints such as oil leaks are justified, but who cares? <P>As for Fieros, I've had two since January, 1984, the longest I've ever had any make.   <P>||||reg||9
Z||000001||wkayl||02-14-2000||11:04 PM||||I have had a 1961 Studebaker Lark XIII Cruiser since 1974.  And it's not just because no one else wants it either.  My son came home from the hospital in it and when he was 12 he drove it on my dad's farm in S Dak (his 1st drive).  It was also the 1st car he drove when he turned 16.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||02-14-2000||11:05 PM||||Also check out Click and Clack's Car-O-Scope. <A HREF="http://cartalk.cars.com/Survey/Results/Psychographics/" TARGET=_blank>http://cartalk.cars.com/Survey/Results/Psychographics/</A> <p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 02-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||02-14-2000||11:36 PM||||I checked out all 883 complaints for 1986 fieros and found about 40% of the failures was due to owner negligence. "engine blew up due to no oil"!! There was a complaint that the "power hatch motor didn't close hatch causing the electrical system to short out" What year Fiero had a power hatch option that closed itself? 1989? I think it was suppose to be a Firebird. Some of the other complaints were the E-brake, Clutch wear, etc. I even saw on that said "engine froze up due to excessive wear" below it stated the car had 317,000 miles on it!  Another one said the clutch wore out due to the flywheel being welded to the crankshaft resulting in vehicle replacement. The list goes on and on. It looks like most complaints are from disgruntled owners who had some moron mechanic work on the car and they messed it up. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-14-2000).]||||reg||1
